{"id":"26795386-7016-4140-8799-b8d6ffca4483","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7edb1c3fc7d88088","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"377a1f38808b96a402685f3e52d82c580be88671","start":5859,"end":6008},"shape":{"type":"AwaitExpression","atoms":["await","vscode",".","workspace",".","fs",".","delete","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","file","(","root","+","\"","/.git","\"",")",",","{","\"","recursive","\"",":","true",",","\"","useTrash","\"",":","false","}",")",".","then","(","undefined",",","(",")","=>","{","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"46932b1e61389a9a","after":"e07e94000ee9586a"}},"payload":{"text":"The workspace's `.git` goes too, though clearWorkspace keeps it as scaffolding: the workspace is becoming\nsomething else. A clone (git-clone.ts) brings its own, history and all; anything else (a sample, a playground, a\nrepo read through the API) gets a fresh one below — kept, the last repo's origin would still be where a commit\npushes, and what the shell takes the workspace for (`git.origin`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:24.966Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:24.966Z"}
{"id":"29781af4-59c6-4a26-bcc9-f596d6a4bb4f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6c058fb0185cc531","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f48548a2c8f44ce513e757f78cfde1d758d24862","start":5300,"end":5424},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","uris","=","entries",".","map","(","(","[","name","]",")","=>","vscode",".","Uri",".","file","(","dir","+","\"","/","\"","+","name",")",")","as","unknown","as","Parameters","<","WorkspaceFs","[","\"","announce","\"","]",">","[","0","]"]},"context":{"before":"52782a7d6b1386c6","after":"c1eb126eed5119ad"}},"payload":{"text":"The extension API's Uri IS vscode's URI class in this (local-process) host — the type the provider fires.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:27.399Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:27.399Z"}
{"id":"299f76fc-82ac-43fb-8c98-94ae936e1c31","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"461d03eb418f456b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0b2002c0c5b7610f395e2ebee8c0ae06aa40ff05","start":8646,"end":8810},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","!","providedAtRoot","(","\"",".gitignore","\"",")",")","{","await","vscode",".","workspace",".","fs",".","writeFile","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","file","(","root","+","\"","/.gitignore","\"",")",",","encoder",".","encode","(","gitEngine",".","DEFAULT_GITIGNORE",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"03014421880facc0","after":"629edf69dcde23f0"}},"payload":{"text":".gitignore: isomorphic-git reads zen-fs directly, so MATERIALIZE the git default when the repo omits it\n(in-place overwrite — clearWorkspace kept it). Matches ensureRepo's first-run default.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:09.912Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:09.912Z"}
{"id":"3109a35c-e8d0-4df5-b642-7984d735dfbf","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8e57b186de6aa7af","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a626a640e95a8ede23f206e587f596bcc2cdb413","start":1781,"end":1853},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","FALLTHROUGH_DEFAULTS","=","new","Set","(","[","\"","tsconfig.json","\"",",","\"","jsconfig.json","\"","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"00a55c0f2211ea2f","after":"e5d2407c37142881"}},"payload":{"text":"Root-level managed configs are OVERRIDABLE DEFAULTS: writable in zen-fs (see workspace-fs.ts), and writable in the\npriority-1 base too (see the boot below) — the file service refuses a write to a path whose stat says read-only, so a\nread-only base would make a deleted default impossible to write again. A write goes to the highest writable overlay,\nzen-fs: the base never changes, and the new file is the workspace's (copy-up). A loaded repo's own copy overwrites in\nplace, because clearWorkspace keeps these. When a repo ships NONE, the reconciliation differs by how the config is read:\n  FALLTHROUGH_DEFAULTS — TS project configs, read by tsserver via the COMPOSITE file service: DELETE the writable\n    copy so the priority-1 base shows through.\n  .gitignore — read straight off zen-fs by isomorphic-git (a priority-1 base would be invisible to it): MATERIALIZE\n    the git default (gitEngine.DEFAULT_GITIGNORE) into zen-fs.\n  ESLINT_CONFIGS — kept overridable so a repo's own is writable; eslint's worker lints with it (else the preset)\n    (extensions/eslint/worker.ts), so there's nothing to materialize; on omit we just drop a stale one. Variants are\n    one concept — a repo providing ANY counts.\nKeep OVERRIDABLE_DEFAULTS in sync with workspace-fs.ts.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:39.811Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:39.811Z"}
{"id":"37ff21a8-b842-4f15-953b-2f49c821de1a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e07e94000ee9586a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"000abf9c2ce1fa99cd3b685fda1cb028d558a8f6","start":6429,"end":6585},"shape":{"type":"AwaitExpression","atoms":["await","vscode",".","workspace",".","fs",".","delete","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","file","(","root","+","\"","/.silo/local","\"",")",",","{","\"","recursive","\"",":","true",",","\"","useTrash","\"",":","false","}",")",".","then","(","undefined",",","(",")","=>","{","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"7edb1c3fc7d88088","after":"2280cedb532e6330"}},"payload":{"text":"And what was kept here about the last one's code (`.silo/local/`: its dependency baseline and what of the code it\nread, its runs, its coverage): kept, the new code's first reading continued the old one's — a clone's every use of\na package the starter also used read as grown.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:22.487Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:22.487Z"}
