{"id":"58ed3ff4-f878-4a76-8f45-8211316e2070","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"649030fe2d566ee6","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"92004fe20d96dc04c9304b36a6ce790b8b001a92","start":7835,"end":7891},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","provided","=","new","Set","(","files",".","map","(","(","file",")","=>","file",".","path",")",")"]},"context":{"before":"33831ae296f6afd6#2","after":"8e41156f710f08c6"}},"payload":{"text":"Reconcile overridable-default configs the loaded repo did NOT provide (the write loop above already\noverwrote any it DID ship; clearWorkspace kept these so those were in-place overwrites).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:15.041Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:15.041Z"}
{"id":"61c76cfa-56d4-4a83-b6f9-cfa1e6289b1c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"93323999d56b443c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7dff126b5e8da54ae0db036491398000fa1a72f4","start":10121,"end":10734},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","followProjectSwitches","(","hub",":","Hub",",","open",":","(","project",":","Project",")","=>","Promise","<","void",">",",","log",":","Logger",")",":","void","{","let","pendingProject",":","Project","|","undefined",";","let","projectTimer",":","ReturnType","<","typeof","setTimeout",">","|","undefined",";","hub",".","subscribe","(","\"","workbench.openProject","\"",",","(","data",")","=>","{","pendingProject","=","data",";","clearTimeout","(","projectTimer",")",";","projectTimer","=","setTimeout","(","(",")","=>","{","const","project","=","pendingProject",";","pendingProject","=","undefined",";","if","(","project","!==","undefined",")","{","void","open","(","project",")",".","catch","(","(","error",":","unknown",")","=>","{","log",".","error","(","\"","openProject failed","\"",",","{","\"","error","\"",":","failureText","(","error",")","}",")",";","}",")",";","}","}",",","150",")",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"e6446dffe7f97e93","after":"318f36fa5370b7e0"}},"payload":{"text":"A live project switch (the shell's repo load → the app → here) arrives as a publish; written and focused into the\nrunning workbench (`open`). `replace` (a GitHub repo load) clears the workspace first — the workspace becomes the\nrepo.\n\nCOALESCED: the hub delivers a single load as a burst of identical publishes. That's harmless for a plain write\n(idempotent), but a `replace` clears + rewrites the SingleBuffer (SAB) FS each time, and repeated clear/rewrite\ncycles corrupt it (\"offset is out of bounds\"). So we debounce the burst to ONE run with the latest request.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:02.419Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:02.419Z"}
{"id":"62a22428-2e7b-496a-acbd-b090f0465e00","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2280cedb532e6330","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9f331eda04500115ef7bf5669591a9325251db0a","start":6883,"end":7200},"shape":{"type":"For","atoms":["for","(","const","file","of","files",")","{","const","dir","=","file",".","path",".","slice","(","0",",","file",".","path",".","lastIndexOf","(","\"","/","\"",")",")",";","if","(","dir",".","length",">","0","&&","!","madeDirs",".","has","(","dir",")",")","{","madeDirs",".","add","(","dir",")",";","workspaceStore",".","mkdirSync","(","dir",",","{","\"","recursive","\"",":","true","}",")",";","}","workspaceStore",".","writeFileSync","(","file",".","path",",","file",".","bytes","??","encoder",".","encode","(","file",".","contents","??","\"","","\"",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"f9465b9622357bb2","after":"37965a60fb8606bc"}},"payload":{"text":"Written straight into the workspace's store, all at once: its change watcher (workspace-changes.ts) reports them\nto VS Code as one batch, as it does isomorphic-git's and the terminal's writes. Through VS Code's file service each\nfile cost a stat to validate it, two mkdirp walks of its folders and a listing of its folder — each a path walk in\nzen-fs, the listings quadratic in a folder's size (288 files in one of this repository's): the page was busy for\nminutes loading a repository of ~2,000 files.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:20.095Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:20.095Z"}
{"id":"71e9858d-9320-4c48-a5cc-a1251c9aacd9","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"00a55c0f2211ea2f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f9893c74aa3572d8f68b93f4f15d8aeeb7a16c45","start":1461,"end":1546},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","SCAFFOLDING","=","new","Set","(","[","\"","editor-ambient.d.ts","\"",",","\"",".silo","\"",",","\"","node_modules","\"",",","\"",".git","\"","]",")"]},"context":{"before":"375f2e1808c1e539","after":"8e57b186de6aa7af"}},"payload":{"text":"Editor-owned paths at the workspace root: the shim .d.ts (when the demo needs one), the capability ledger,\nacquired deps, git meta. They survive a `replace` (the editor needs them) and are never sent back to a repo on commit.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:42.208Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:42.208Z"}
{"id":"7373c413-1c11-486a-a3ec-b6f6ae291caa","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"56e65951c98ec5b1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"46c09ead870b7f0d9198bcd3ec8780a441ef0ebb","start":1021,"end":1070},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","workspaceStore","=","callerFs","(","store",",","\"","project","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"1bc489029e29c318","after":"375f2e1808c1e539"}},"payload":{"text":"The workspace's store as a project is written into it: its calls the project's, in the store's counts (fs-caller.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:44.570Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:44.570Z"}
{"id":"a531f181-3b4e-4760-95b7-72cc134109b8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"629edf69dcde23f0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1cb26ece272b1ccc2a45cb74e257c9728914f372","start":9015,"end":9163},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","files",".","some","(","(","file",")","=>","file",".","path",".","startsWith","(","root","+","\"","/.git/","\"",")",")",")","{","await","gitEngine",".","includeSilo","(",")",";","}","else","{","await","gitEngine",".","ensureRepo","(",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"461d03eb418f456b","after":"57161a03b39ae9f2"}},"payload":{"text":"A load that brought its own `.git` (a clone): `.silo/` goes in git there too. Any other: a new repository, no\none's origin.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:07.448Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:07.448Z"}
{"id":"c0c7461c-bb84-4441-886c-94b3855f59ec","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2ba0211f4c65b4d8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"54c0cbff190ac99ed85be192bbc12bfcc7629bd3","start":12947,"end":13309},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","serveOrigin","(","hub",":","Hub",")",":","void","{","serve","(","hub",",","\"","git.origin","\"",",","async","(",")","=>","{","const","[","owner",",","repo","]","=","/","github\\.com\\/(.+)\\.git$","/","u",".","exec","(","await","gitEngine",".","githubRemote","(",")","??","\"","","\"",")","?.","[","1","]",".","split","(","\"","/","\"",")","??","[","]",";","return","owner","===","undefined","||","repo","===","undefined","?","null",":","{","\"","owner","\"",":","owner",",","\"","repo","\"",":","repo",",","\"","branch","\"",":","(","await","gitEngine",".","branches","(",")",")",".","current","??","\"","main","\"","}",";","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"318f36fa5370b7e0"}},"payload":{"text":"The GitHub repository the workspace is a clone of — its origin, and the branch it's on — or null, as `git.origin`: the\nshell's binding (where a commit pushes, what an `env/` address compares with), read from the workspace so the two\ncan't disagree.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:59:57.319Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:59:57.319Z"}
{"id":"cf581094-cdf2-4f9e-8e15-ec9ff066abef","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"70d693898908d13c2695e48639252a569834dd00","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"A project loaded into the live workbench — a repository from GitHub (repo-load.tsx), or a sample: its files written\ninto the workspace's store all at once and its editors opened, without a reboot. A `replace` clears the workspace\nfirst — the workspace becomes the repository — keeping the editor's scaffolding and reconciling the configs the\neditor provides as defaults. A load arrives as `workbench.openProject` (followProjectSwitches); the boot opens its\nfirst editors the same way.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:49.306Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:49.306Z"}
{"id":"d977f328-317e-43b0-9d21-230fe83da214","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e7bce4efd90f1399","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a8874bd7464aea6f895cff7689f478b8b0ad3428","start":4418,"end":4601},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","!","kept","(","name",")",")","{","await","vscode",".","workspace",".","fs",".","delete","(","vscode",".","Uri",".","file","(","root","+","\"","/","\"","+","name",")",",","{","\"","recursive","\"",":","true",",","\"","useTrash","\"",":","false","}",")",".","then","(","undefined",",","(",")","=>","{","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"bb5770d72820d95a#1","after":"bf933a38437ea290"}},"payload":{"text":"Keep scaffolding always; keep overridable-default configs so a repo that ships its own can OVERWRITE them\nin place (openProject prunes the ones the repo omits afterwards, so those fall through to the base).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:32.373Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:32.373Z"}
{"id":"e342eb13-b140-4262-b051-88271d845522","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"29b2be577fb37d4b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/project.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d9e74e770758a24feaa1286dceeb5709c9214396","start":3734,"end":4055},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","going","=","vscode",".","window",".","tabGroups",".","all",".","flatMap","(","(","group",")","=>","group",".","tabs",")",".","filter","(","(","tab",")","=>","{","const","path",":","string","|","undefined","=","tab",".","input","instanceof","vscode",".","TabInputText","?","tab",".","input",".","uri",".","path",":","undefined",";","return","path","?.","startsWith","(","root","+","\"","/","\"",")","===","true","&&","!","tab",".","isDirty","&&","!","kept","(","path",".","slice","(","root",".","length","+","1",")",".","split","(","\"","/","\"",")","[","0","]",")",";","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"795e2d36e77c5910","after":"f5138b66805a623d"}},"payload":{"text":"Close the editors on the files about to go first. VS Code closes an editor whose file is deleted from inside the\napp, but a moment later — after a load has reopened the same file in that editor, which then closes instead.\nUnsaved editors stay, as VS Code keeps them.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:34.789Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:00:34.789Z"}
